# EnvironmentPostProcessor is not an autoconfiguration: it runs before the
# context exists, so it cannot be registered through AutoConfiguration.imports.
# spring.factories is still the mechanism for this one specific hook in Boot 4,
# and registering it in the wrong file is silent - the defaults simply never
# apply, and every service quietly runs on Boot's own defaults instead.
#
# Note the package: org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor, not
# org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor. Boot 4 deprecated the
# latter for removal and moved the interface up a package.
org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
com.payorch.infra.observability.ObservabilityDefaults
